<section class="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
      <div id="q1">
        <h3><a href="#q1">Will I get banned from GTA:Online for playing NSM?</a></h3>
        <p>Nope! NSM does not modify your Grand Theft Auto V installation files and never interacts with Rockstar Online Services other than validating your game ownership on startup.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="q2">
        <h3><a href="#q2">How do I sign in inside NSM.exe?</a></h3>
        <p>Click <strong>Sign in</strong> inside <code>NSM.exe</code>. It will open the NSM website in your browser where you can sign in to your AFX account and automatically link your session back into <code>NSM.exe</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="q3">
        <h3><a href="#q3">How do I create a server and register a license key?</a></h3>
        <p>Open <a href="/keymaster">AFX Portal</a>, sign in to your account, generate a <code>cfxk_...</code> license key, and paste <code>sv_licenseKey</code> into your server's <code>server.cfg</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="q4">
        <h3><a href="#q4">Why does Steam show me playing Source SDK Base 2007?</a></h3>
        <p>Like the classic modification runtime, NSM initializes Steam integrations under App ID <code>218</code> (<strong>Source SDK Base 2007</strong>) so your Steam overlay, friends list, and rich presence work cleanly without conflicting with the base game.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

